Depth is not communicated through traditional shadows, but through **Tonal =
Layering** and **Glassmorphism**.

1.&nbsp; **Level 0 (Background):** Solid Deep Space Blue or Void Black.
2.&nbsp; **Level 1 (Containers):** Semi-transparent (10-20% opacity) surfac=
es with a `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)`.
3.&nbsp; **Level 2 (Active/Hover):** Inner glows using &quot;Cyan Glow&quot=
; or &quot;Galactic Purple&quot; at low opacity.
4.&nbsp; **Borders:** All elevated containers must have a 1px &quot;ghost b=
order&quot;=E2=80=94a semi-transparent white or cyan stroke that defines th=
e edge of the glass surface.

Shadows, when used, are &quot;Ambient Glows&quot; that inherit the color of=
 the element (e.g., a purple button emits a purple aura, not a black shadow=
